hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17937","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani, he said, Abu Anabah narrated to me, Surayj said, and he had companionship, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, When Allah Almighty intends good for a servant, He honeys him. It was said, What is His honeying him. He said, Allah Almighty opens for him a righteous deed before his death, then takes him upon it."
"17938","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said, Shurahbil ibn Muslim al-Khawlani narrated to me, he said, I saw seven men, five had accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and two had eaten blood in the pre-Islamic age and had not accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). As for the two who had not accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they are Abu Anabah al-Khawlani and Abu Fatih al-Anmari."
"17939","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani, he said, Martyrs were mentioned before Abu Anabah al-Khawlani, and they mentioned one who dies of belly disease, plague, and a woman in childbirth. Abu Anabah became angry and said, The companions of our Prophet narrated to us from our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said, The martyrs of Allah on earth are the trustees of Allah on earth among His creation, whether killed or dead."
"17940","al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, he said, al-Jarrah ibn Malih al-Bahrani, a Humsi, informed us, from Bakr ibn Zarah al-Khawlani, he said, I heard Abu Anabah al-Khawlani say, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, Allah Almighty will continue to plant in this religion plantings He employs in His obedience."
